# Sahayi Subscription Service — stack and layout

TypeScript + Express 5 microservice. Architecture reference: sibling `Sahayi_User_Service/`. Do not add this work to User Service. Do not introduce JS files, mysql2, Mongoose, Flyway, awilix, or `/api/v1` route prefixes.

## Stack

- Node.js 20, Express 5, TypeScript (strict)
- Prisma 7 + MariaDB adapter (`libs/db/src/prisma.ts`)
- Zod (`libs/validation/src/validate.ts`)
- Pino, JWT auth
- Default port `SUBSCRIPTION_SERVICE_PORT` **3007**

## Folders

```
src/routes controllers services repositories validators types
src/middlewares clients openapi errors
src/container.ts  src/app.ts  src/server.ts
libs/             config db logger auth validation response
prisma/schema.prisma
generated/prisma  never edit
```

## Naming

| Artefact | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Files | kebab-case | `subscription.service.ts` |
| Classes | PascalCase | `SubscriptionService` |
| Methods | camelCase | `listSubscriptions` |
| Env vars | UPPER_SNAKE | `SUBSCRIPTION_SERVICE_PORT` |
| Prisma fields | match DB (`Id`, `Name`) | |
| API DTOs | camelCase | `{ id, name, monthlyCost }` |

Logs use `service: 'subscription-service'`. Follow the feature slice in `011-feature-slice.mdc`.
